  "name": "Chegança (Northeastern nautical folk drama)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Sailors' folk drama of the Northeastern coast, strongest in Sergipe around Laranjeiras and also found in Alagoas and Bahia, in which a troupe in naval uniforms (marujos) re-enacts a voyage and a sea battle between Christians and Moors in sung scenes while playing tambourines. Related nautical plays called barca, fandango or marujada stage the ballad of the Nau Catarineta, a ship adrift at sea. A source-unspecified pandero card stands in for the marujos' tambourines.",
